.TH "GLESHA-STATE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-state \- move existing state out of the config directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha state migrate [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move existing state out of the config directory.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B migrate
Move legacy local state to the current location.
.IP
No cloud access is required. Archive files move without re\-encryption. Empty legacy registries need no migration. Existing destinations are not merged; use \-\-state\-dir to select a fresh destination.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global options
.TP
.B \-\-format FORMAT
Result format: plain or json; status also supports table and csv (default: plain).
.TP
.B \-\-progress MODE
Progress on stderr: auto, plain, or off (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
TOML settings file.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir DIR
Local state directory; overrides catalog.directory.
.TP
.B \-\-env FILE
Load credentials; existing process variables take priority.
.TP
.B \-\-color MODE
Color mode: auto, yes, or no (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-log\-level LEVEL
Diagnostic verbosity: debug, info, warn, error, or silent (default: info).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show this command's help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version and build revision.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha state migrate
glesha list \-\-state\-dir /path/to/state
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
Results and tables go to stdout. Activity, prompts, warnings, and errors go to stderr.
Use \-\-format=json for version 2 result records, one per line.
JSON diagnostics and progress use separate version 1 records on stderr; neither stream contains ANSI controls.
Use \-\-progress=off to disable progress. In plain output, redirected stderr or TERM=dumb uses step lines.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1)
